1. A method for printing letters using a line thermal head, the method comprising:
receiving input data representing characters to be printed;
generating a plurality of print data rows, each print data row corresponding to a scan line of a character image;
providing a print medium adjacent to a line thermal head, the line thermal head comprising a plurality of heating elements extending across a print width;
sequentially moving the print medium relative to the line thermal head;
for each of the plurality of print data rows, selectively activating a subset of the plurality of heating elements based on the corresponding print data row while the print medium is moved, thereby forming a line of dots on the print medium; and
repeating the sequential moving and the selective activating for each of the plurality of print data rows to form one or more complete letters on the print medium.

