A system for efficient hardware implementation of a perfect precision blending function, comprising:
an input interface configured to receive a plurality of input data operands, each having a defined input precision, and at least one blending factor having a defined blending factor precision;
a blending processing unit coupled to said input interface, said blending processing unit comprising dedicated hardware logic circuitry configured to:
    generate a first intermediate product by multiplying a first input data operand from said plurality of input data operands by said at least one blending factor;
    generate a second intermediate product by multiplying a second input data operand from said plurality of input data operands by a complement of said at least one blending factor;
    generate a preliminary blended result by adding said first intermediate product and said second intermediate product; and
    scale said preliminary blended result to a target output precision;
    wherein said dedicated hardware logic circuitry is configured to maintain an intermediate precision for said first intermediate product, said second intermediate product, and said preliminary blended result that is sufficient to prevent loss of significant bits from said input data operands and said blending factor during said multiplying and adding operations, thereby ensuring perfect precision blending; and
an output interface coupled to said blending processing unit, said output interface configured to provide a blended output data operand having said target output precision.

