A method for compressing motion vectors of an unsynchronized picture, the method comprising:
    receiving motion vectors corresponding to blocks of an unsynchronized picture, wherein the unsynchronized picture is characterized by a lack of a standard temporal reference frame for motion vector prediction;
    determining, for a current block within the unsynchronized picture, a predicted motion vector for a current motion vector of said current block, said predicted motion vector being based on at least one of spatially neighboring motion vectors within the unsynchronized picture or motion vectors from a non-temporally aligned reference source;
    generating a motion vector difference by subtracting the predicted motion vector from the current motion vector; and
    encoding the motion vector difference to produce compressed motion vector data associated with the unsynchronized picture.

An automatic control circuit for enabling and disabling a supply voltage to a short-range wireless device, the circuit comprising:
