1. An electric vehicle propulsion system comprising:
    a battery pack including multiple solid-state rechargeable electrochemical cells;
    at least one electric motor electrically coupled to the battery pack, which is configured to generate propulsion for an electric vehicle;
    an inverter electrically coupled between the battery pack and the at least one electric motor, the inverter arranged to convert direct current (DC) power from the battery pack into alternating current (AC) power for driving the at least one electric motor;
    a controller electrically coupled to the battery pack, the inverter, and the at least one electric motor, the controller adapted to manage power transfer between the battery pack and the at least one electric motor, and to oversee operation of the at least one electric motor; and
    a charging interface electrically coupled to the battery pack, the charging interface adapted to accept external electrical power to replenish the multiple solid-state rechargeable electrochemical cells.

A method for polymerizing an α-olefin, comprising:
contacting at least one α-olefin monomer with a catalyst system in a reaction zone;
wherein said catalyst system includes a transition metal compound and an activator;
operating said reaction zone at an effective polymerization temperature of from about 0°C to about 200°C and an effective polymerization pressure of from about 1 bar to about 100 bar;
and obtaining a poly-α-olefin therefrom.

1. A metallic ink jet printing system adapted for graphics applications, comprising:
    an ink jet printhead configured to eject metallic ink droplets;
    an ink supply system fluidically coupled to the ink jet printhead and holding a metallic ink composition;
    a substrate transport mechanism arranged to position a substrate relative to the ink jet printhead for printing;
    a controller coupled to the ink jet printhead and the substrate transport mechanism, the controller configured to receive graphics data and generate control signals for directing the ink jet printhead to selectively eject the metallic ink composition onto the substrate, thereby forming a metallic graphic consistent with the graphics data; and
    a curing apparatus positioned to treat the metallic ink composition deposited on the substrate to fixate the metallic graphic.
